      "start_seconds": 246.6,
      "end_seconds": 254.89,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now severe hypothermia is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.67,
      "end_seconds": 282.26,
      "duration_seconds": 13.59,
      "text": "we should do blood tests for hypothermia we should do a blood sugar for hypothermia handle gently and warm slowly with warm blankets and and warm fluids through the drip"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.58,
      "end_seconds": 294.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.36,
      "text": "Mm, okay. I'd like you to see the emergency team as well, and I'll write the referral. One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait."
